WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.285
The audit read asks Graph's directory
audit log for one window at a time:

2
00:00:04.285 --> 00:00:07.279
everything PIM logged,
plus the role assignments

3
00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:10.200
the directory logs when
someone goes around PIM.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.513
It goes through the same
careful reader as Chapter 1,

5
00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.133
refuses a window older than the log keeps,

6
00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:20.525
and starts each window where the last
one ended, so no hour goes unread.

7
00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:22.850
It keeps IDs and drops names.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.599
Then four checks: a role assigned
outside PIM, a sensitive activation with

9
00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:32.500
no approval, someone approving their
own request, and a PIM setting changed.
